<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pallars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pallars is a historic region of the Catalan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> around the valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noguera-pallaresa">Noguera Pallaresa</a> river. Once a district of the Frankish county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, it became a hereditary county under Ramon I around 872 and was divided in 1011 into Pallars Jussà and Pallars Sobirà. The names survive in two modern Catalan districts with their capitals at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tremp">Tremp</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sort">Sort</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pallars.jpg" alt="Pallars" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MARIA ROSA FERRE ✿ · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fili%C3%A0_-_5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
